        <div class="faq">
          <div class="faq__item"><button class="faq__q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q1">How often should I clean my solar panels?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button><div class="faq__a" id="q1"><div>In most cases, solar panels benefit from a clean once or twice a year. The right frequency depends on your location, climate and surroundings — if your panels are in an area with heavy dust, pollen or bird droppings, more frequent cleaning may be needed.</div></div></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><button class="faq__q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q2">Do dirty solar panels really reduce energy production?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button><div class="faq__a" id="q2"><div>Yes. Dust, dirt, bird droppings and other debris block sunlight from reaching the cells, which reduces output. A regular clean helps your panels operate at their highest efficiency.</div></div></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><button class="faq__q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q3">Can I clean my solar panels myself or should I hire a professional?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button><div class="faq__a" id="q3"><div>You can clean them yourself, but we highly recommend a professional who's experienced working at heights. We also know how to keep your system within warranty by using the correct tools, and we do a wiring check to make sure your panels are fully operating.</div></div></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><button class="faq__q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q4">How do you clean solar panels safely?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button><div class="faq__a" id="q4"><div>We use deionised (pure) water and soft brushes with proper height-safety equipment, so we remove dust, grime and bird droppings without scratching the panels or voiding warranties.</div></div></div>
